The campaign board decides that a decade-long infrastructure programme is a bad
subject for a four-week campaign, and that whichever way we lean we will lose
somebody. The material goes to print without it.

Both large parties are delighted to have the field. PiS runs on the betrayal of
a Polish investment; the liberal centre runs on managing it competently. Between
those two stories there was a third one about who owns the thing and who builds
it, and this month we decide not to tell it.

